{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The original proof repeatedly unpacks bisimilarity into its witness relation and duplicates symmetric transition-matching code. Bisimilarity’s `follow_fst` and `follow_snd` methods already return bisimilar derivatives, allowing a direct construction with substantially less syntax and elaboration work.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro h\\n  use @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs, ChoiceBisim.choice h\\n  intro s1 s2 hr μ\\n  constructor\\n  · intro s1' htr\\n    cases hr with\\n    | choice h =>\\n      cases htr with\\n      | choiceL htr =>\\n        obtain ⟨q', htr', h'⟩ := h.follow_fst htr\\n        exact ⟨q', Tr.choiceL htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR htr =>\\n        exact ⟨s1', Tr.choiceR htr, ChoiceBisim.bisim HomBisimilarity.refl⟩\\n    | bisim h =>\\n      obtain ⟨s2', htr', h'⟩ := h.follow_fst htr\\n      exact ⟨s2', htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n  · intro s2' htr\\n    cases hr with\\n    | choice h =>\\n      cases htr with\\n      | choiceL htr =>\\n        obtain ⟨p', htr', h'⟩ := h.follow_snd htr\\n        exact ⟨p', Tr.choiceL htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR htr =>\\n        exact ⟨s2', Tr.choiceR htr, ChoiceBisim.bisim HomBisimilarity.refl⟩\\n    | bisim h =>\\n      obtain ⟨s1', htr', h'⟩ := h.follow_snd htr\\n      exact ⟨s1', htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\"}"}}
